# Materials Library — Single Source Of Truth

## Authoritative file (as of v2.3.3)

The single source of truth for all indexed PBR materials is:

**Local (SketchUp plugins folder):**
`C:\Users\Administrator\AppData\Roaming\SketchUp\SketchUp 2026\SketchUp\Plugins\Na__Common__DataLib__CoreSuEntityStandards\Na__DataLib__CoreIndex__Materials__.json`

**GitHub raw URL (fetched by TrueVision at runtime):**
`https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Adam-Noble-01/Plugins/main/Na__Common__DataLib__CoreSuEntityStandards/Na__DataLib__CoreIndex__Materials__.json`

**GitHub repo:**
`https://github.com/Adam-Noble-01/Plugins/tree/main/Na__Common__DataLib__CoreSuEntityStandards`

The local `Na__AppConfig__MaterialsLibrary.json` that previously lived inside the TrueVision CoreAppCode repo has been **deleted**. Do not recreate it.

TrueVision fetches this file at startup via `AppCore__DataLib__Loader.js` (`Na__DataLib__LoadAll()`). The materials data is available throughout the app via `Na__DataLib__GetMaterials()`. The root key inside the JSON is `Na__DataLib__CoreIndex__Materials`.

Do **not** invent ad-hoc material names in Ruby exporters, hardware JSON, or renderer code without a matching entry in the DataLib file above.


## Mandatory registration

Any **new SketchUp material name** (the material `display_name` used in SketchUp) that must participate in **indexed** PBR substitution, GLB export naming, or web-renderer lookup **must** be added to `Na__DataLib__CoreIndex__Materials__.json` in the SketchUp plugins repo.


## Naming convention
- Format: `MAT{NNN}__{Category}__{Variant}...` — **three digits** after `MAT`, then `__`.
- `SketchUpName` in JSON **must** match the SketchUp material display name **exactly** (character-for-character).
- The runtime treats names matching `/^MAT\d{3}__/` as indexed materials (`Na__MaterialsSystem__IsIndexedName`).


## Series layout (high level)
- **MAT000** — defaults / template  
- **MAT010** — modeling utilities  
- **MAT100** — basic (glass, wood, mirror, plant foliage MAT160, plant stem MAT161)  
- **MAT300** — paint  
- **MAT500** — timber  
- **MAT600** — metals: generic / galvanised / structural / aluminium (**MAT600–MAT603**), **MAT604–MAT610 reserved**, ironmongery finishes from **MAT611**.

New metals or ironmongery finishes: extend `MAT600__MetalSeries__` following existing keys; assign the next free code.


## Workflow for new materials
1. Choose the next **MAT###** code and full `SketchUpName` string.
2. Add an entry to `Na__DataLib__CoreIndex__Materials__.json` under the correct series; only specify keys that differ from the `MAT001__Default` template.
3. Create or rename the SketchUp material so its name matches `SketchUpName` exactly.
4. Bump `meta.version` and `meta.lastUpdated` in the DataLib file.
5. No TrueVision web-app file needs updating — `AppCore__DataLib__Loader.js` fetches from GitHub automatically.
